[I] A backup program for disk arrays

[T] SnapRAID is a backup program designed for disk arrays, storing parity
[T] information for data recovery in the event of up to six disk failures.
[T] Primarily intended for home media centers with large, infrequently
[T] changing files, it works with disks already filled with data and hashes
[T] all data to detect silent corruption.

[U] https://www.snapraid.it

[A] Snapraid Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

